{
  "item": "R1",
  "scores": {"U": 3, "A": 2, "C": 3, "V": 2},
  "confidences": {"U": 0.7, "A": 0.8, "C": 0.7, "V": 0.8},
  "rationales": {
    "U": "证据片段：'Inter departments:', 'DA group member', 'faculty group member', 'higher level group' – 解释：关键术语如'DA group'和'higher level group'未定义，上下文模糊，导致需求难以理解。",
    "A": "证据片段：'must be approved by a DA group member and faculty group member unless it came from a higher level group' – 解释：'and'可能表示同时需要或逻辑与，'unless'子句条件不明确（例如，批准是否仍需进行），存在歧义。",
    "C": "证据片段：'unless it came from a higher level group' – 解释：除非子句可能使'必须批准'的要求在特定情况下矛盾或无效，逻辑关系不清晰，潜在正确性问题。",
    "V": "证据片段：'DA group member', 'faculty group member', 'higher level group' – 解释：这些组未定义，批准操作未指定（如如何验证批准），无法设计可测试的用例。"
  },
  "suggestions": {
    "U": "将需求改写为：'跨部门请求必须由DA组成员和教工组成员批准，除非请求来自更高级别组。'并添加术语定义部分。",
    "A": "消除歧义：'对于跨部门请求，必须同时获得DA组成员和教工组成员的批准。但如果请求是由比当前部门更高级别的组发起，则此批准要求不适用。'",
    "C": "明确逻辑：'跨部门请求需由DA组和教工组批准；然而，若请求来源为上级组，则无需此类批准。'",
    "V": "使可测试：定义DA组、教工组和更高级别组，并指定批准为系统中的一个确认步骤。例如：'DA组指数据管理组，教工组指教学人员组，更高级别组指上级管理部门。跨部门请求必须由这两组成员在系统中批准，除非来自管理部门。'"
  },
  "issues": [
    {"type": "U", "evidence": "Inter departments: request must be approved by a DA group member and faculty group member unless it came from a higher level group", "rewrite": "跨部门请求必须由DA组成员和教工组成员批准，除非请求来自更高级别组。"},
    {"type": "A", "evidence": "must be approved by a DA group member and faculty group member unless it came from a higher level group", "rewrite": "必须同时获得DA组成员和教工组成员的批准。但如果请求是由更高级别组发起的，则此批准要求豁免。"},
    {"type": "C", "evidence": "unless it came from a higher level group", "rewrite": "但如果请求来源是更高级别组，则无需DA组和教工组的批准。"},
    {"type": "V", "evidence": "DA group member, faculty group member, higher level group", "rewrite": "定义DA组为数据管理组，教工组为教学人员组，更高级别组为上级管理部门。批准需在系统中记录确认。"}
  ]
}

{
  "item": "R1",
  "scores": {"U": 2, "A": 2, "C": 3, "V": 1},
  "confidences": {"U": 0.9, "A": 0.95, "C": 0.8, "V": 0.95},
  "rationales": {"U":"'Inter departments' is ambiguous phrasing — it lacks subject and grammatical role; 'request must be approved by a DA group member and faculty group member unless it came from a higher level group' contains undefined terms ('DA group', 'faculty group', 'higher level group') and no scoping (e.g., which departments? what constitutes 'inter-departmental'?). Evidence: 'Inter departments' and 'higher level group'.","A":"'unless it came from a higher level group' introduces conditional logic without defining the set of valid groups or hierarchy rules; 'a DA group member and faculty group member' is ambiguous — does this mean one person who belongs to both groups, or two distinct persons? Evidence: 'a DA group member and faculty group member' and 'higher level group'.","C":"The requirement may be logically incomplete: approval by two roles is mandated for inter-departmental requests, but no exception handling is specified for cases where either role is unavailable; however, no internal contradiction is evident, so correctness score is moderate. Evidence: 'must be approved by a DA group member and faculty group member unless...' implies a policy intent but lacks completeness.","V":"No testable acceptance criteria: undefined entities ('DA group', 'faculty group', 'higher level group'), no measurable condition for 'inter departments', and no observable pass/fail outcome. A test cannot determine whether a request 'came from a higher level group' without a formal, enumerated list or authoritative source. Evidence: 'unless it came from a higher level group'."},
  "suggestions": {"U":"Replace with: 'For any request originating in one department and targeting resources or actions in another department, the following approval rules apply.'","A":"Replace with: 'Each inter-departmental request must receive explicit approval from exactly two individuals: one designated as a Data Authority (DA) role holder and one designated as a Faculty Governance role holder, both assigned to the requesting or target department; this dual-approval requirement is waived only if the request originates from an organization explicitly listed in Appendix A as a Tier-1 authority.'","C":"Keep unchanged — the core policy intent is plausible; however, completeness should be addressed in supplementary requirements.","V":"Replace with: 'The system shall log the organizational unit ID of the request originator; if that ID matches any value in the read-only Tier-1 Authorities list (Appendix A), then no DA/Faculty approval is required; otherwise, the system shall enforce that exactly two non-revoked approvals are recorded — one with role = ''DataAuthority'' and one with role = ''FacultyGovernance'' — before allowing request progression.'"},
  "issues": [
    {"type":"U","evidence":"Inter departments","rewrite":"For any request originating in one department and targeting resources or actions in another department, the following approval rules apply."},
    {"type":"A","evidence":"a DA group member and faculty group member unless it came from a higher level group","rewrite":"Each inter-departmental request must receive explicit approval from exactly two individuals: one designated as a Data Authority (DA) role holder and one designated as a Faculty Governance role holder, both assigned to the requesting or target department; this dual-approval requirement is waived only if the request originates from an organization explicitly listed in Appendix A as a Tier-1 authority."},
    {"type":"V","evidence":"unless it came from a higher level group","rewrite":"The system shall log the organizational unit ID of the request originator; if that ID matches any value in the read-only Tier-1 Authorities list (Appendix A), then no DA/Faculty approval is required; otherwise, the system shall enforce that exactly two non-revoked approvals are recorded — one with role = ''DataAuthority'' and one with role = ''FacultyGovernance'' — before allowing request progression."}
  ]
}
